# GENERATED, and so not source. Every number in these is read from the
# file that owns it -- the board, the design, or the ISP's own published
# contract -- and build.sh regenerates all of them before Vivado starts.
# Committed, they would be a second copy of facts that already have
# owners, going stale in silence the first time someone edits an owner
# and does not rebuild. That disagreement does not surface as an error:
# a width mismatch in a block design is a CRITICAL WARNING and a quiet
# connection of the low bits.
hdl/generated/
boards/*/generated/
board-files
vivado-library
build/
out/
*.jou
*.log
*.bit
*.hwh
.Xil/
NA/
# dvi2rgb writes its timing tables beside the board while it elaborates
# and removes them again. They exist only during a build, which is
# exactly when someone is most likely to stage everything.
boards/*/dgl_*.data
clockInfo.txt
tight_setup_hold_pins.txt
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
